{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1485121-question-about-grappling","id":1485121,"title":"Question about grappling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-27T10:38:40-07:00","id":1485121,"title":"Question about grappling","content":"When you are grappling with someone, and you manage an exceptional success, you can choose to do 2 moves from the list of moves, and its great.<br /> <br /> However, if I choose to do damage 2 times (with my 2 moves)... the other guy is allowed to try to roll his Str + Brawl also the 2 times, possibly delivering damage to me on the second try (second move) ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T10:48:09-07:00","id":1485122,"title":"","content":"For starters, I really have doubts about you being able to choose the same maneuver.<br /> <br /> In any case, you use the success from the first Str+Brawl that net you the Exceptional Success. So, for example, if you have 6 success over the opponent, you will do 6 damage two times (again, if your Storyteller let you use the same maneuver two times, I certainly not)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T13:41:24-07:00","id":1485141,"title":"","content":"While the phrasing isn't as solidly done as it could be, the wording is that you pick one move from the list, or two moves from the list with an exceptional success. Picking two moves without further wording technically parses to &quot;pick two different moves,&quot; as picking the same move twice isn't actually picking two moves from the list.<br /> <br /> And, even if that wasn't the technical reading, double damage would be obnoxiously potent considering how grappling already works. As altidiya said, it would essentially double your damage. And even more so for werewolves, if they use a bite to damage in a grapple, they get to add their bite weapon damage on top of their successes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}